    "description": "Different addictions may look completely different on the surface - alcohol, gambling, social media, work - but underneath, they follow the same repeating mecha",
    "h1": "The Core Pattern Behind All Addictions",
    "sections": [
      {
        "h2": "Overview",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Different addictions may look completely different on the surface – alcohol, gambling, social media, work – but underneath, they follow the same repeating mechanism."
        ],
        "h3Items": [],
        "bullets": []
      },
      {
        "h2": "The universal addiction loop",
        "paragraphs": [
          "At the center of almost every addiction is a reinforced behavioral cycle:"
        ],
        "h3Items": [
          {
            "h3": "1. Trigger (Cue)",
            "body": "Something creates discomfort or urge"
          },
          {
            "h3": "2. Craving (Urge)",
            "body": "The brain remembers: “This worked before”"
          },
          {
            "h3": "3. Behavior (Action)",
            "body": "You act to relieve the craving"
          },
          {
            "h3": "4. Reward (Relief / Pleasure)",
            "body": "This is the hook"
          },
          {
            "h3": "5. Reinforcement (Learning)",
            "body": "The loop becomes faster and more automatic"
          },
          {
            "h3": "6. Consequences → Repeat",
            "body": "And the cycle continues"
          }
        ],
        "bullets": [
          "Stress, boredom, loneliness, habit, environment",
          "Internal (emotion) or external (situation)",
          "Desire to change how you feel",
          "Anticipation of relief or reward",
          "Drinking, scrolling, gambling, eating, etc.",
          "Dopamine release",
          "Temporary relief, escape, or stimulation",
          "Brain strengthens the pathway",
          "“Next time, do this again”",
          "Guilt, fatigue, stress, withdrawal",
          "These often become the next trigger"
        ]
      },
      {
        "h2": "How different addictions fit the same loop",
        "paragraphs": [
